Sval: a permission says whether the defaults file grants it

The permission manager keeps the entries it imports from
permissions.manager.defaultsUrl apart from the profile's own
(cIDPermissionIsDefault): it never removes or expires them, and restores one
when the profile's entry that replaced it is removed. nsIPermission does not
carry that, so the Sites settings could not tell a grant Sval ships from one
the user made. isDefault carries it on the permissions getPermissionObject,
getAll and getAllForPrincipal return.

